{"id": "development/a-dense-chronological-account-of-human-learning", "title": "A Dense, Chronological Account of Human Learning", "group": "development", "parent": null, "source": "2c_data.tex", "line": 77, "children": ["development/structural-overview", "development/a-dense-chronological-account-of-human-learning-overview", "development/higher-level-overview", "development/even-higher-level-overview", "development/from-conception-to-birth", "development/0-3-months", "development/3-6-months", "development/6-12-months", "development/12-24-months", "development/2-3-years", "development/3-4-years", "development/4-5-years", "development/5-7-years", "development/7-9-years", "development/9-12-years", "development/12-25-years", "development/neural-development"], "level": 1, "domain": "", "part": "", "construction": false, "editorialCount": 0, "excerpt": "Giving an on-average account Main things to answer in each subsection 1. What are the behavioral capabilities acquired at this stage? (what are the behavioral developmental milestones) 2. What are the dominant objectives (and resulting error signals / training", "html": "<div class=\"manuscript-children\">\n<div class=\"manuscript-paragraph\"><p>Giving an on-average account</p></div>\n<div class=\"manuscript-paragraph\"><p>Main things to answer in each subsection</p></div>\n</div>\n<p>1. What are the behavioral capabilities acquired at this stage? (what are the behavioral developmental milestones) 2. What are the dominant objectives (and resulting error signals / training data) supporting these behavioral advancements, and how does each optimizer come into play? (what are the learning algorithms that produce the aforementioned behavioral advancements?) 3. What does the child understand about the world at this stage? (the cognitive results of the training algorithm; relate back to key cognitive development concepts) 4. How do the brain’s macroscopic activity patterns and structural properties develop at this stage? (the neurocomputational perspective; relate back to key neurodevelopmental concepts) 5. How is this stage of learning made possible by previous stage (neurally, cognitively, and behaviorally)?</p>\n<section class=\"domain-map\"><h2 id=\"age-domain-map\">Age × domain map</h2><p class=\"map-note\">From age 4 each stage is written up domain by domain, then as the training data and optimization behind it and its neural development. Earlier stages are written up as a whole. Read across a row for one stage, or down a column to follow a domain through development.</p><div aria-label=\"Age by domain map\" class=\"table-scroll\" role=\"region\" tabindex=\"0\"><table class=\"domain-grid\"><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Stage</th><th>Language</th><th>Semantic &amp; episodic memory</th><th>Social</th><th>Physics, objects &amp; tools</th><th>Motor</th><th>Spatial</th><th>Causal learning &amp; simulation</th><th>Executive function</th><th>Post-formal thought</th><th scope=\"col\">Training data and optimization</th><th scope=\"col\">Neural development</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\"><a href=\"#/article/development/from-conception-to-birth\">From Conception to Birth</a></th><td class=\"all-domains\" colspan=\"9\"><a href=\"#/article/development/from-conception-to-birth\">Described as a whole</a></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\"><a href=\"#/article/development/0-3-months\">0–3 months</a></th><td class=\"all-domains\" colspan=\"9\"><a href=\"#/article/development/0-3-months@behavioral-capabilities\">All domains together</a></td><td><a aria-label=\"Training data and optimization, 0–3 months\" href=\"#/article/development/0-3-months@training-data-and-optimization\">Read</a></td><td><a aria-label=\"Neural development, 0–3 months\" href=\"#/article/development/0-3-months@neural-development\">Read</a></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\"><a href=\"#/article/development/3-6-months\">3–6 months</a></th><td class=\"all-domains\" colspan=\"9\"><a href=\"#/article/development/3-